Package: baxters-vs-mic-widget
Version: 1.0.1-2
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Baxters Lab <165753632+Baxterv5@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-tk, ffmpeg, xdotool
Recommends: wl-clipboard, xclip
Suggests: xsel
Description: VS Mic Widget — offline floating speech-to-text
 A small always-on-top widget that records from the microphone, transcribes
 with whisper.cpp locally, and copies or types the result into whichever window
 you chose as the target. Nothing leaves the machine.
 .
 DISTRO interpreter lane (A1 section 2a): Tkinter is a distro C-extension bound
 to the system interpreter, so this does not use baxters-runtime.
 .
 xdotool is a hard dependency, not optional: it is how the widget identifies the
 paste target and types into it. Without it the widget starts and every paste
 silently fails with "xdotool error" in the status line.
 .
 xclip is Recommends and xsel Suggests because the widget tries them in order
 and degrades honestly: with neither, Copy stops working while recording and
 transcription still do.
 .
 whisper.cpp is NOT packaged and is deliberately not a dependency. The widget
 expects whisper-cli and a model under the user's home, and says so in its
 status line when they are absent. Packaging a multi-gigabyte model is a
 separate decision (see the release readiness notes).
